Go module dependencies

No third-party Go source is vendored into this repository; go.mod and go.sum are
the whole list, and the release image's SBOM (RELEASE.md §3) is the authoritative
one for a build. Every module in that list is under a permissive licence — MIT,
Apache-2.0 or BSD-3-Clause — with no copyleft anywhere in the graph. The check is
one command, and it is a release precondition:

  go install github.com/google/go-licenses@latest
  go-licenses report ./...

The tracing dependencies are named here rather than left to go.mod alone, because
they are the ones an operator switches on from configuration, and turning them on
sends request metadata to a collector somebody else runs: go.opentelemetry.io/otel
and its sdk, metric and trace/noop packages,
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace and its otlptracehttp client,
go.opentelemetry.io/proto/otlp and go.opentelemetry.io/auto/sdk are Apache-2.0;
google.golang.org/protobuf, which the OTLP client pulls in, is BSD-3-Clause. None
of them is copyleft, and none ships a NOTICE file of its own to carry forward.
